 "effect_check": "weaker",
 "effect_summary_en": "Lau et al. (2013, England) link local thoracic surgeons to higher lung cancer resection rates: 20.0% in hospitals where surgeons were based vs 11.6% in peripheral hospitals. The study is observational, and the abstract does not show the 2.4-point figure for surgeons attending the lung meeting.",
 "supported_en": "Lau et al. 2013 report a lung cancer resection rate of 20.0% in English hospitals where surgeons were based vs 11.6% in peripheral hospitals.",
